WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Female Merc</b>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.010
<b>Nobu</b>

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.430
<b>Léontine du Louv 
Mercenary for Oilia</b>

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:54.440
I wonder what that person does.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.940
<b>Hermina (16)
Waitress at Nobu.
Berthold's wife</b>

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.530
I bet she's a mercenary.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:57.560
A mercenary?

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.100
Her tough look and that armor 
chest, there's no doubt about it.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.550
You're so knowledgeable.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.860
Shinobu-chan, the appetizer is ready.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:05.630
Coming.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.980
Here's your draft beer and an 
appetizer of stewed egg cockles.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.170
Thank you.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.950
<b>Stewed Egg Cockles</b>

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.950
<b>These stewed egg cockles 
have a great texture. Enjoy.</b>

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.940
Pretty fancy to get an amuse-gueule.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.890
Amuse-gueule?

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.450
It's a snack that's served before the meal.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:28.450
Hm. It's a mussel, but it's texture 
is closer to that of chicken.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.710
It's not fishy, and it's taken 
on the fond's flavor well.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.460
Quite nice.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.350
Thank you very much.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:38.130
Next, I'll try Aitheria's ale.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.410
<b>Fizz</b>

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.810
It's so nice and cold. And this feeling 
when it goes down your throat...

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:50.190
It's so pleasant. I've never 
had an ale like this before.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.760
Did you like our whatsontap?

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.740
So this ale is called whatsontap?

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.410
Yes, that's what our regulars call it.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.020
Shinobu-chan, can I have a whatsontap 
and a seafood broth please?

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.400
I'll have the "almost bouillabaisse."

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:05.800
Coming right up.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:11.950
Ah, so that's what I smelled 
in front of this place.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:16.550
Would you like some of the broth 
and the "almost bouillabaisse"?

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.560
I can imagine what a seafood broth is.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.950
<b>Ushiojiru</b>

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.950
<b>Hermina's special fisherman's taste. The bones 
and the clams give this seafood broth a nice taste.</b>

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.950
It's a soup cooked from the bony parts 
of a fish and seasoned with salt, right?

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.340
And the other thing, is it made with tomato?

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:27.260
<b>Almost Bouillabaisse</b>

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:27.260
<b>If you've made too much broth, 
be brave and change direction.
 The tomato flavor seeps in nicely.</b>

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:28.790
Yes. We briefly fry the vegetables, 
then cook them together with

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.740
various seafood and tomatoes.

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:33.600
I made too much of the broth,

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.720
so Taishou cooked it together with the 
tomatoes to change up the look a bit.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.710
Ah, that's why it's called 
"almost bouillabaisse."

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:45.730
No disrespect to you, but I'll have that.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:50.300
Thank you so much. Taishou, 
one bouillabaisse please!

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.340
Roger.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.500
Oh, Hermina-chan, can you 
help me wash the dishes?

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.820
Oh, sure.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.770
<i>Gentle and cheerful.</i>

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.260
<i>They're so completely different from someone 
who's lived on the battlefield like me.</i>

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:11.010
<i>But if I hadn't been a mercenary, 
I might have been married by now,</i>

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:18.000
<i>making a rockfish tomato stew for 
my husband in a tiny kitchen.</i>

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.610
Thank you for waiting.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.180
Your "almost bouillabaisse."

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.650
Oh, this looks good.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.140
It's hot, so please be careful.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.690
<i>The shrimp and seafood umami 
has really permeated the soup.</i>

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.530
<i>It brings back memories.</i>

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.030
<i>A gentle flavor that reminds 
me of the ocean back home.</i>

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.180
How do you like it?

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.160
It's quite good for an improvisation.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:53.190
Where I come from, we use saffron 
and tomato to cook the fish,

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.530
but this isn't bad.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.050
So, you come from 
a fishing town as well?

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.940
Please call me Léontine.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:04.720
I grew up in a city by the 
sea in the south of Oilia.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.470
You, too?

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:10.740
My name is Hermina. I come 
from the northern sea.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.730
I just got married and that's 
why I'm in Aitheria.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.530
I see, that's quite the change then.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:19.600
Are you here for work, Léontine-san?

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:24.710
Yes, I'm on my way north to work 
as a guard for Lord Windelmark.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:28.570
However, I need to find 
a man before I do that.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.250
You're looking for someone?

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.070
Yeah.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:36.630
A really skilled man they called 
"the Devil" on the battlefield.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:44.370
It was a couple of years back, an icky 
day with foggy rain when I met that man.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:48.900
The ground was so soaked that 
our feet sunk in to our ankles.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:53.370
Under those conditions, the Devil came 
at us by himself, like a whirlwind.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:57.890
He was only wearing minimal armor.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:01.140
It was certainly a benefit 
under those conditions,

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:04.360
but if he had been dealt even one 
blow, it would have cost his life.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:07.510
It's not something you can do if you're 
not absolutely sure of yourself.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.740
Don't let this life go waste.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:37.270
I've come to this city to repay that debt.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:41.040
Léontine-san, your helmet 
adornment is a squid, right?

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.650
It's unusual, right?

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:46.410
That's why the people from my home 
don't put squid into our tomato stew.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.160
It's bad luck.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.470
The person Léontine-san is looking 
for is Berthold-san, right?

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:54.290
Yeah, definitely.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:58.900
What are you going to do when 
you do find this Devil-san?

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.940
I can't tell you that.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.940
At this rate,

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:11.780
she's going to have a duel with him when 
Berthold-san comes to pick Hermina up.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.080
Shinobu-chan, please go outside and—

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.620
<b>Berthold (32)
 Company Commander of 
Aitheria Palace Guards aka "the Devil"</b>

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.630
Hey, I'm here!

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.790
You guys enjoying your drinks?

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.020
Hm? Who are you?

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:28.040
Please don't provoke her!

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.260
Huh? Provoke?

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.500
You're the Devil, right?

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.640
Oh, are you the one with the squid helmet?

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:42.500
You remembered me?

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.370
How could I forget?

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:48.110
There are not that many female 
mercenaries as good as you.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:51.560
Do you remember this? You gave it to me.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:55.740
You were so strong. All right! 
This is some sort of fate.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.550
Let's drink together tonight!

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:01.400
I never expected to meet you here.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.060
I'm Berthold.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:08.850
I'm Léontine. I'm glad you're doing well.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.750
Hermina, I'll have a whatsontap.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:12.480
Right away.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.910
Should we call Nikolaus-san and the others?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.830
You two, it'll be okay.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:17.710
But...

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:22.210
The thing Léontine-san is wearing 
around her neck is a love charm.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.640
A love charm?

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:28.100
She's looking for someone 
with that charm— Wait!

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:31.100
Then what if she finds out 
that you're his wife?!

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:34.500
If I were her, it would be quite hard for me.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.280
Wh-What should we do?

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:38.190
Shinobu-chan, calm down.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.740
Anyway, I need go bring the drink out.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.500
R-Right.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:48.130
The weather that day was horrible.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.490
Here is your beer.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.110
Oh, thanks.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.620
Let me introduce you. 
This is my wife, Hermina.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.120
He just said it!

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.080
W-Wife?

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.770
Yeah, we just got married.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.760
Isn't she pretty?

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.890
You shouldn't...

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.020
I see.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.460
Something wrong?

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:18.960
Of course.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.760
It's been years since that day.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:26.340
There's nothing weird about that ridiculously
strong Devil having a family by now.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:27.640
R-Right.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:31.910
Berthold, are you happy right now?

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:35.560
Yeah. Happy as can be. Couldn't be better.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:36.980
I see.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:41.710
All right, everyone. Next round is on me.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:44.230
Hermina, please bring everyone a whatsontap.

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:45.340
Okay.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.090
Are you sure?

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:50.320
Yeah, I'm feeling generous today.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.850
Léontine-san?

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:56.340
May I have something, too?

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:59.250
Of course.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.360
Let's have a toast.

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:07.370
To meeting again— No, to 
celebrate your happy marriage.

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.630
Yes, thank you.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.020
Prosit!

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.800
Taishou, thanks!

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.620
Shinobu-chan, I'll come again.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.150
Please do.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.370
It was fun tonight. Thank you.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:24.330
Yeah.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:28.280
Marriage is great. You should find 
yourself a good man soon, too.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:30.410
Okay. Got it.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.220
Shall we?

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:34.170
Yes. Taishou, I'm taking off.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.960
See you tomorrow.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.210
Léontine.

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:39.280
Take care.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:43.130
You, too.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.310
Shall we head home?

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.210
Yes.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.590
She was pretty.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:57.020
Oh, really?

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.310
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.960
Here you go.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.040
This is on the house.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:23.740
Salty.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up, we have Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:39.380
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:39.380
We're recreating the popular French dish 
with ingredients any household will have.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:45.050
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:46.370
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.150
Léontine-san was such a good person.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:51.310
<b>Léontine</b>

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:49.630
Yes, really noble.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.930
I could fall for someone like her.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:52.520
The way she pulled back?

00:10:51.510 --> 00:11:00.550
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:10:51.980 --> 00:11:00.550
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:53.500
It put tears in my eyes.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:58.670
And when she told the 
staff, "next round's on me"?

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.200
That generosity was so cool!

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.100
It really was.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.200
And what are we making today?

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:06.950
I think making bouillabaisse 
at home is a tad too hard.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:07.830
Completely impossible.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:11.840
Today I'd like to make a 
bouillabaisse-like soup that can be

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:15.550
made with things that every 
household probably has.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:16.400
<b>Easy bouillabaisse that can be made
 with things you have at home</b>

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:16.410
That makes me so happy.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:18.150
This is for my Léontine-san.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:18.880
She's yours now?

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:23.870
<b>Bouillabaisse from boiled 
mackerel and sakura shrimp

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:21.880
Let's see, boiled mackerel 
and sakura shrimp.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.880
You can make bouillabaisse with that?

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:26.600
The garlic should be like 
this, with its skin.

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:51.400
<b>Bouillabaisse from boiled 
mackerel and sakura shrimp</b>

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.870
Put the knife on it and hit it like this.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:29.840
Bam, bam.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.880
Then the skin comes right off.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.570
That's so easy.

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:36.100
After that, we just chop it up coarsely.

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:37.250
Got it.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.100
We chop the onion as well.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:45.470
We put the chopped garlic in the pot.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:45.770
The stove isn't even on. Is that okay?

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:48.580
One tablespoon of olive oil.

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.420
Just toss that in.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:55.320
Since garlic burns easily, start 
frying it when the pot's still cold.

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:55.940
<b>Put the garlic in the pot 
before turning up the heat</b>

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.420
I didn't know that.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:57.880
Adding the onion now.

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:03.660
Once the onion starts to get 
soft, we add the sakura shrimp.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:04.620
Roger.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.420
Since I want the umami from the shrimp 
to really transfer to the soup,

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:10.700
I'm going to crush
the shrimp a bit here.

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.720
<b>Roughly crush the sakura 
shrimp to get the umami out</b>

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.740
I see!

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.190
And now the white wine.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:16.670
Oh, that smells good!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:20.340
When you add white wine to seafood 
dishes, it cuts that fishy smell.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.030
True.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.860
And the water of this canned mackerel

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.690
has tons of umami in it,

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:28.740
<b>Add the canned mackerel with the water</b>

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:27.090
so we're going to add the 
whole can to the pot.

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:29.020
So today's dish has a Japanese touch.

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:31.150
Lightly break the meat apart.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:33.700
Sort of cutting the pieces 
in half with the spatula.

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:35.600
Now the tomato juice.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.020
It'll give it a nice finish.

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:39.530
I'm so glad it stayed simple!

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.660
Plain water.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:42.870
Some salt.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.620
It's starting to look like bouillabaisse!

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:48.310
Once it's boiling, lower the heat and 
let it cook for about five minutes.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:50.040
Add some pepper.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:54.940
And, only if you have 
this, some dried herbs.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.190
It'll add authenticity to the dish.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:58.660
I'm using oregano today.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.760
That looks like a hit.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.670
I'm going to let that cook 
for about five minutes now.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.050
It's done!

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.160
That's looking good!

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:08.160
Canned mackerel and sakura shrimp are 
usually available in the pantry,

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:16.510
<b>Bouillabaisse from boiled 
mackerel and sakura shrimp</b>

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:13.220
and they happen to be jam-packed with umami.

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:16.510
Of course, I think adding clam or squid 
or other seafood would be good too,

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:19.750
but it's more casual this way, 
so please do try it at home!

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:33.000
<b>Today's high-speed footage</b>

